WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.400
One of Mexico's most iconic species,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.760
the Monarch butterfly, has just lost

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.513
perhaps its greatest advocate.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.920
If we are to analyze Homero's death,

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.520
he was saying things that perhaps

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.830
other people didn't want to listen to

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.770
and he was also dealing with people

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:36.110
linked to organized crime.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.550
Homero Gomez, the manager of the sanctuary

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.250
was found dead after police say

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.070
he was beaten and thrown down a well.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.770
His family says he had
recently received threats

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:48.903
warning him to stop the campaign
against illegal logging.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:12.000
Because the police
investigation has been so opaque

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.840
and because people are so fearful to speak

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.920
and tell journalists the truth

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.010
because of the kind of society of fear,

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.360
which has been created around
speaking truth to power,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.370
then it is likely that
we might not ever know

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.930
why Homero ended up in an irrigation ditch

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.822
in late January, 2020.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.240
The Monarch butterfly migration is one

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.053
of the most impressive natural
phenomena in the world.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.050
Every year, swarms of black
and orange-colored butterflies,

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.080
about the size of a small kind of saucer

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.080
travel 2,500 miles from
North America, Canada area,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.300
all the way to the
forest of Central Mexico.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.760
The Rosario sanctuary where
the story sort of takes place

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.350
is in the state of Michoacán.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.990
It's a protected area
with tremendous amounts

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.150
of woodland, mainly pine.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.410
It's a very beautiful and
very sort of singular area

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.210
within Mexico, geographically
and biologically speaking.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:25.470
Homero was a local to the area

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.780
to La Huella Rosario,
which is in Michoacán.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.790
He grew up with the Monarchs

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.360
and actually his
grandparents often told him

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.200
that the Monarchs were effectively

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.113
the spirits of his ancestors.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.020
When you've got an area like a biosphere,

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.190
which is obviously a very fertile place

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.860
with a lots of natural resources,

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.280
you have all sorts of conflicts.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.570
So you have people that want to use

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.220
the trees for logging,

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.010
you know, both legal and illegal.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.820
When there's so much money at stake

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.710
and there's all this
land which could be used,

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:48.933
then yes, there are conflicting interests.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.560
Homero and his family worked
in the timber industry

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.180
and the local environment,

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.680
which they inhabited was their
biggest economic resource.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.560
So when the biosphere was formed

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.930
or certain parts of it were
protected over the years,

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.570
Homero wasn't necessarily in favor.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.140
However, as the international
community came in

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.050
and the scientists were sort of observing

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.290
this natural phenomenon,

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.960
which is an incredible thing to witness,

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.240
I think he began to see the butterfly

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.600
as something extremely important

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.190
and a way that could not
only preserve the way of life

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.950
that he had become used
to and the community,

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.260
but was something that was

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.440
of national, international importance.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.920
He then became one of
their biggest advocates

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.750
and became an extremely important figure,

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.760
both nationally and internationally

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.940
for the protection and
the diffusion of the story

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.240
of the Monarch butterfly
in Mexico and abroad.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.760
He was a larger than life person.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.710
There's a Spanish expression
called, Don de jentes,

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.980
which is like a person who really has,

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.200
you know, a way with people.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.510
You know, he could, he
was charismatic, charming,

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.450
and he was the type of person that

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:22.700
if they went to a local event,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.498
all the local politicians would know him.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.950
He really was an advocate
for the butterfly

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.670
and worked extremely
hard to tell their story.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.730
He wouldn't take no for an answer.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.660
I think he rubbed up a
lot of local politicians,

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.350
the wrong way, as well
as the local scientists.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.530
He had friends in powerful places as well.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.160
And I think that was just
the nature of his job.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.600
When one wants to rise to become
a public figure in Mexico,

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.400
and one is willing to
criticize people openly

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.130
or even not criticize,

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:57.430
but sort of fight against certain aims,

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:00.300
then he or she puts himself at risk.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.190
The south west state of Michoacán

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.233
is where Mexico's drug war began.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.120
Michoacán state where the story took place

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.610
is probably one of the
most dangerous states

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.530
in Mexico, at present.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:13.860
There's lots of drug routes.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.160
It's full of natural resources.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.713
And also it is the epicenter
for the avocado trade.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.410
What's happening now in
Mexico is very interesting.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.110
Cartels are moving towards

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.940
almost legitimizing themselves in a way.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:31.010
So they're moving into ordinary businesses

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.360
and they're moving into
things like avocado trade,

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.760
which is an incredibly lucrative trade

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.660
worth about $2.4 billion annually

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.780
and 80% of the avocados that are imported,

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.080
in the United States,
come from Mexico itself.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.390
The cartels will come in
and use physical violence,

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.960
wipe farmers off their land,

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.410
take over the land and therefore

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.260
infiltrate themselves into the trade.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.220
There's almost like a civil war

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.190
between the drug cartels
in Michoacan state.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:01.210
So everyone's fighting for
the drug smuggling routes,

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:04.440
the avocado trade, the natural resources.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.470
And what happens when you exist in a state

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.240
in which the authorities are corruptible

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.590
is very easy to infiltrate these areas.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.950
And you've seen that a lot in
the Western part of the state

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.950
where the tactics have
almost become medieval.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.320
People hanging from bridges, massacres,

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.590
kidnappings of big avocado farmers,

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.740
just because there's
so much money at play.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.260
Where the sanctuary itself is situated

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.220
is further to the east.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.540
So it's near the state of Mexico

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:34.410
closer to Mexico City itself.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.420
And that area isn't too
effected by organized crime.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:40.040
but even so they're kind of the shadow,

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.580
the looming nature of organized crime

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.990
means that people are always
wary of talking to outsiders.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.630
Homero's wife, Rebecca, lived
in a constant state of fear

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.730
because she knew where she lived.

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:53.380
And she said that she
would often tell him,

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:54.370
you know, please be careful.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.410
And he said, "No, no, no.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.860
These people are my friends."

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.970
Around midday on January 13th,

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.713
Homero Gomez attended what
would be his last meeting.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.690
It was an ordinary meeting.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.823
It was to take place in the
butterfly sanctuary at Rosario.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.100
The only thing that people really remember

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.540
from that meeting in fact is that

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.860
Homero himself was receiving
constant phone calls.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.620
His phone was buzzing constantly,
constantly, constantly.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.620
According to some of the people
who attended that meeting,

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.180
he eventually picked up the phone

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:02.070
and the other person on
the other end of the line

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:06.180
was trying to convince
him to go to a local event

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.120
in a town called El Soldado,

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.220
where there was like a local kind of fair.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:14.570
I think there was horse
racing, drinking, eating,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.030
a local kind of party where

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.160
a lot of the local politicians would be,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.320
activists, you know, people that Homero

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.800
normally kind of hung
around with, so to speak.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.630
And he arrived according to his family

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.240
and to other people
that attended the event

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.870
in El Soldado around about 4 or 5 pm.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.050
There he met with local politicians

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.680
and they described him
as being kind of normal,

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.593
his normal charismatic self.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:43.130
And then it was around about 7, 8 pm,

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:45.240
that one of the
politicians that I spoke to

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.073
who was at the event,

00:09:46.073 --> 00:09:47.220
saw him for the last time.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.270
Obviously, people became very worried

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:56.750
because in Mexico, if
someone goes missing,

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.560
then it's obviously a bad sign.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.230
And that's when his wife, particularly,

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.430
began to worry because she knew very well

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:05.210
the types of people that
Homero hung around with,

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.353
who he dealt with.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.410
The next day, they
reported it to the police.

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:11.120
The police said that they
would take it very seriously

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.770
because he was a public person.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.270
Within, you know, a matter of days,

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.550
search parties were formed

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.390
in which the family took part in,

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.100
the national police, the local police.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.720
I think even the federal police

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.003
actually, helped in these searches.

00:10:41.908 --> 00:10:45.130
The days went on and the
search party searched,

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.050
kept searching, kept
searching, kept searching,

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:48.150
and nothing was found.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.820
That was until the 29th of January,

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:56.460
when a local shepherd found

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.410
the body of Homero Gomez

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.620
in an irrigation ditch,

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:03.280
which was about 150 meters

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.853
from where the local fair
had been taking place.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:10.010
One of the search brigades
had searched that area

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:12.790
about a week before and they'd
found absolutely nothing.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.400
Homero's son told me that
people had even thrown

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.320
stones down into the irrigation ditch

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.223
to check to see if there
was anything there.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.640
And while the police kind
of kept quiet about this,

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.150
that led a lot of people to suspect

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:37.153
that the body had been
put there, after the fact.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.090
When the police came out

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.870
and offered their official
statement on the case,

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.990
they said that the body had
received blunt head trauma

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:50.223
and had been strangled or asphyxiated.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.590
However, they weren't
willing to say, definitively,

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.900
that this had been a murder.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.470
It could have been an accident.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:00.040
While the family weren't obviously,

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.330
willing to believe this,

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:03.510
Homero Jr. himself told
me on many occasions

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:05.460
that he thinks his father was murdered.

00:12:53.551 --> 00:12:54.950
I regularly check in with the family

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:57.220
and they say that there has
been no update in the case

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.470
that no one really has
been in contact with them.

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:02.873
That the police seemingly
have sort of forgotten.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.910
Being an activist is a
very dangerous thing to be.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.700
Quite a few activists
in the last few years

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.900
have been murdered for the message

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.370
that they're trying to
spread in the same way

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.030
that journalists there are often murdered

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.700
for trying to do their job

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.040
or having become involved in corruption.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.270
And I think what that says about the state

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:31.770
is that if you want to
speak out against power

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.110
or illicit activities,

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:36.050
it's one of the most dangerous
things that you can do.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:38.570
Because the police
investigation has been so opaque

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.430
and because people are so fearful to speak

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:42.380
and tell journalists the truth,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.410
then it is likely that
we might not ever know

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:48.010
why he ended up in an irrigation ditch

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.523
in late January, 2020.

